{
  "dom_id": "step-q95778",
  "name": "Question 9",
  "problem": "Given that the random variable $X∼B(75,0.55),$ use the normal approximation to the binomial distribution to approximate $P(X=37).$ Give your final answer to three decimal places\n\n*Hint: The data below is taken from the table of values of the cumulative distribution function $Φ(z)$ for the standard normal distribution. *\n\n<table align=\"center\">\n\n<tbody><tr>\n<th>\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"5\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr> <th width=\"25%\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$z$</th><th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,0.00\\,$</th><th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,0.01\\,$</th><th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,0.02\\,$</th>\n</tr><tr> <th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,-1.2\\,$</th><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.1151\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.1131\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.1112\\,$ </td></tr>\n<tr> <th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,-1.1\\,$</th><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.1357\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.1335\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.1314\\,$ </td></tr>\n<tr> <th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,-1.0\\,$</th><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.1587\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.1562\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.1539\\,$ </td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</th>\n\n<th width=\"5%\"></th>\n\n<th>\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"5\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr> <th width=\"25%\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$z$</th><th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,0.06\\,$</th><th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,0.07\\,$</th><th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,0.08\\,$</th>\n</tr><tr> <th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,-0.9\\,$</th><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.1685\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.1660\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.1635\\,$ </td></tr>\n<tr> <th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,-0.8\\,$</th><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.1949\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.1922\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.1894\\,$ </td></tr>\n<tr> <th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,-0.7\\,$</th><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.2236\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.2206\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.2177\\,$ </td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</th>\n</tr>\n\n</tbody></table>",
  "worked_solution": "Given a binomial random variable $X∼B(n,p),$ if \n\n- $np>5,$ and\n\n- $n(1-p)>5,$\n\nwe can approximate $X$ as a normal random variable $Y$ with mean $\\mu =np$ and variance ${\\sigma }^{2}=np(1-p),$ that is, \n\n$$\nY∼N(np,np(1-p)).\n$$\n\nHere, we have $n=75$ and $p=0.55.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}np & =75\\cdot 0.55 \\\\  & =41.25 \\\\  & >5\\,✓ \\\\ n(1-p) & =75\\cdot (1-0.55) \\\\  & =33.75 \\\\  & >5.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we can approximate our binomial random variable $X$ with a normal random variable $Y$ with mean\n\n$$\n\\mu =np=(75)(0.55)=41.25\n$$\n\nand variance\n\n$$\n{\\sigma }^{2}=np(1-p)=(75)(0.55)(1-0.55)=18.56.\n$$\n\nThat is, we can approximate $X$ by $Y∼N(41.25,18.56).$\n\nNow, we can approximate the desired probability $P(X=37).$ Using a continuity correction, we have\n\n$$\nP(X=37)≈P(36.5\\le Y\\le 37.5).\n$$\n\nTo compute this probability, we transform to a standard normal random variable by $z$-scoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(36.5\\le Y\\le 37.5) & =P(\\frac{36.5-41.25}{\\sqrt{18.56}}\\le Z\\le \\frac{37.5-41.25}{\\sqrt{18.56}}) \\\\  & ≈P(-1.10\\le Z\\le -0.87) \\\\  & =P(Z\\le -0.87)-P(Z<-1.10) \\\\  & =P(Z\\le -0.87)-P(Z\\le -1.10) \\\\  & =Φ(-0.87)-Φ(-1.10) \\\\  & =0.1922-0.1357 \\\\  & =0.0565\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nP(X=37)≈0.057\n$$\n\nNote: Using a software package for the approximation gives a probability of $0.0569.$",
